{"id": "EUVD-2026-97726", "enisaUuid": "465a642b-b04a-3221-b250-9f8635e23fa7", "description": "An out-of-bounds write vulnerability in the SPI host command interface of Semtech's LR11xx transceiver firmware where a crafted SPI host command with an oversized length field can cause the firmware to write up to 254 arbitrary bytes past the bounds of an internal, non-persistent memory buffer. Exploitation requires physical access to the device and logical access to the SPI bus.", "datePublished": "2026-10-12T17:16:27", "dateUpdated": "2026-10-15T18:04:54", "baseScore": 5.2, "baseScoreVersion": "4.0", "baseScoreVector": "CVSS:4.0/AV:P/AC:L/AT:N/PR:N/UI:N/VC:N/VI:H/VA:H/SC:N/SI:N/SA:N/R:U/RE:M", "references": ["https://www.semtech.com/company/security/security-bulletins/sem-psa-2026-002-lr11xx-security-advisory"], "aliases": ["GHSA-p9mw-jx6h-2wjg", "CVE-2026-6232"], "assigner": "Semtech", "epss": 0.17, "enisaIdProduct": [{"id": "3da184e5-6bf7-3a23-9872-a00f07d01f61", "product": {"name": "LR1121 Transceiver", "vendor": {"name": "Semtech"}}, "product_version": "0 <0x0105"}, {"id": "42da043c-3a5e-36d4-bf0e-d45dc10a05fa", "product": {"name": "LR1120 Transceiver", "vendor": {"name": "Semtech"}}, "product_version": "0 <0x0203"}, {"id": "81163793-a143-3786-a208-9b40ebd92352", "product": {"name": "LR1110 Transceiver", "vendor": {"name": "Semtech"}}, "product_version": "0 <0x0403"}, {"id": "b35367e5-331f-32da-ab6d-f222edba1ed3", "product": {"name": "LR1110 Modem-e", "vendor": {"name": "Semtech"}}, "product_version": "0 <2.1.1"}, {"id": "e62393c7-ee3c-34c0-92d0-7cbcf0cf2f27", "product": {"name": "LR1121 Modem-e", "vendor": {"name": "Semtech"}}, "product_version": "0 <2.1.1"}], "enisaIdVendor": [{"id": "662b9332-ea31-3815-a7bf-5e9a751905b7", "vendor": {"name": "Semtech"}}], "isExploited": false}